<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Book of Joshua</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Book of Joshua is the sixth book of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a>, describing the Israelite conquest and division of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canaan">Canaan</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moses">Moses</a>' successor Joshua. Its accounts of the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jericho">Jericho</a>, Ai and Hazor were long read as history, but archaeology shows a more complex picture, and most scholars regard the book as composed centuries after the events it describes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/book-of-joshua.jpg" alt="Book of Joshua" width="320" height="187" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Papyrus_with_the_fragments_of_the_Book_of_Joshua_(CBL_Cpt_2019.8a).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
